+---
+id: dl-003-validate-complete-json-patch-documents-before-evaluation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate complete JSON Patch documents before evaluation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` must accept only JSON Patch documents and preserve RFC 6902 operation semantics. The
+existing implementation permits non-JSON structure around otherwise usable operation members and
+implements array `replace` as insertion.
+
+## Decision
+
+Deep-clone and validate the complete patch document before evaluation, while continuing to ignore
+unrecognised operation members as RFC 6902 requires. Implement `replace` as a replacement at an
+existing target, rather than reusing the insertion behavior of `add` for arrays.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Patches with non-JSON container structure fail before evaluation, extra valid JSON operation
+members remain harmless, and array replacement no longer changes the array length. Applying a
+failing patch remains atomic to callers because all work occurs on a cloned document.
